description:
Design a 4-bit binary counter that increments its value on each rising edge of the clock (CLK). The counter resets to zero when the reset signal (RST) is asserted. The current count value is output through a 4-bit wide output (Q). This module serves as a basic sequential counter, suitable for applications requiring counting functionality in various digital systems.
module top_module(
  input CLK, RST,
  output [3:0] Q
);

code:
module top_module(
  input CLK, RST,
  output [3:0] Q
);reg [3:0] count;

  always @(posedge CLK) begin
    if (RST) begin
      count <= 4'b0000;
    end else begin
      count <= count + 1;
    end
  end

  assign Q = count;

endmodule

