Design a circuit that implements a pipelined population count for a 255-bit input. The module processes the input in multiple stages, sequentially summing groups of bits to produce a final count of the number of '1' bits in the input vector. The output is an 8-bit wide value representing this count. The design employs a series of adders to aggregate the count throughout the pipeline stages, utilizing registers to store intermediate results before producing the final count.
