description:
Develop a circuit that counts the number of high bits (logic 1s) in a 32-bit input vector. The output is a 6-bit register that represents this count. The design iterates through each bit of the input vector and increments the count for each bit that is high, providing a final tally capable of representing counts from 0 to 32.
module top_module(
    input [31:0] in_vector,
    output reg [5:0] out_count
);

code:
module top_module(
    input [31:0] in_vector,
    output reg [5:0] out_count
);integer i;
    reg [5:0] count;

    always @(*) begin
        count = 0;
        for (i = 0; i < 32; i = i + 1) begin
            if (in_vector[i] == 1) begin
                count = count + 1;
            end
        end
        out_count = count;
    end

endmodule

